# kibi(7)

## NAME

kibi - WASI support and the kibi extensions

## DESCRIPTION

Programs are WebAssembly modules that use WASI preview 1 (p1, `wasi_snapshot_preview1`). Only commands (modules that export `_start`) run. Command components of WASI preview 2 (components that export `wasi:cli/run@0.2.x`) also run, but they can import only `wasi:*@0.2.x`, keep a thread while they wait, and their state is not saved. WASI preview 3 is not implemented yet and fails at load time with `NOEXEC`.

Features that WASI does not have are provided as WIT packages named `kibi:*`. Every package is `@0.1.0`, and only an exact version match is accepted. p1 programs get their functions as imports named `kibi:PACKAGE/INTERFACE@VERSION`.

## PACKAGES

- `kibi:kernel`: event queues (`events`) and timers (`timers`)
- `kibi:process`: start, wait for and kill processes; the working directory; the process list
- `kibi:io`: duplicating file descriptors, pipes, and the terminal (`tty`: raw mode, size, foreground)
- `kibi:fs`: mounting disks and listing mounts and disks (`mounts`)
- `kibi:computer`: free memory (`memory`), uptime and game time (`clock`), power (`power`)
- `kibi:device`: listing and using devices (`bus`)

## NOTES

p2, p3 and the Component Model are thin layers over the same kernel, and they will use the same `kibi:*` WIT. p2 commands (components that export `wasi:cli/run`) run with exec, but they cannot import `kibi:*` yet (`NOEXEC`); p3 and the rest will be added later. The interfaces whose names end in `-poll`, `-async` or `-streams` are provisional ones for p2 and p3; p1 programs cannot import them (`NOEXEC`).

Sockets are not implemented. The p1 `sock_*` functions return `NOSYS`.

The full definitions are the WIT files of the mod and its system call reference (`docs/syscalls/` in the source). Lua programs use these through the `peripheral`, `os` and `parallel` libraries (peripheral(3), os(3), parallel(3)).

